import view.dl

to get UI surface [point] {UI point:point} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if view's fitted:
        set point's x to view's content bounds' x + (point's x * (view's content bounds' width / view's logical width))
        set point's y to view's content bounds' y + (point's y * (view's content bounds' height / view's logical height))
    return point

to save the model transform in {UI frame:frame}:
    set saved to @intrinsic("construct", saved UI transform, frame's view's transform, frame's view's saved transforms)
    set frame's view's saved transforms to storage for one slot initialized with saved

to restore the model transform in {UI frame:frame}:
    set saved to frame's view's saved transforms
    set frame's view's transform to saved's value
    set frame's view's saved transforms to saved's next
    deallocate saved

to move the model in {UI frame:frame} by x {a value:x}, y {a value:y} and z {a value:z}:
    set transform to the address of (frame's view's transform)
    set transform's x to transform's x + (transform's xx * x + transform's xy * y)
    set transform's y to transform's y + (transform's yx * x + transform's yy * y)

to scale the model in {UI frame:frame} by x {a value:x}, y {a value:y} and z {a value:z}:
    set transform to the address of (frame's view's transform)
    set transform's xx to transform's xx * x
    set transform's yx to transform's yx * x
    set transform's xy to transform's xy * y
    set transform's yy to transform's yy * y

to rotate the model in {UI frame:frame} by {a value:angle} degrees around x {a value:x}, y {a value:y} and z {a value:z}:
    require condition ((x = 0.0) and (y = 0.0)) reporting "UI transforms rotate in the surface plane"
    set radians to angle * 0.017453292519943295
    set cosine to the cosine of radians
    set sine to the sine of radians
    set old to frame's view's transform
    set transform to the address of (frame's view's transform)
    set transform's xx to old's xx * cosine + old's xy * sine
    set transform's xy to old's xy * cosine - old's xx * sine
    set transform's yx to old's yx * cosine + old's yy * sine
    set transform's yy to old's yy * cosine - old's yx * sine
